lisa-design:
- Unset = empty string for strings and null for booleans/integers (schema type [x, null]) so an explicit false/0-like value can still be rendered and the API defaults stay authoritative otherwise. Only CCF_STRICT_DISABLE_PUBLIC_AGENT_ENDPOINTS always renders (spec: default false).
- Integers go through int64 before toString: YAML numbers arrive as float64 and would render as 1.6777216e+07.
- First-class keys yield to api.extraConfig (the helper unsets any key extraConfig sets) to avoid duplicate ConfigMap keys and keep installs that already used extraConfig unchanged.
- No validation of instancePruneSchedule beyond string: River's 6-field cron is validated by the API.
